---
mm: 1.2
kind: sdk
name: linux-aarch64
target: aarch64-linux-gnu
compiler-family: any
runtime: glibc
platform-provider: platform.linux.map platform.linux.defaults
platform-provider: mm.stdio platform.linux.stdio
platform-provider: mm.mcu platform.linux.mcu
platform-provider: mm.rtc platform.linux.rtc
platform-provider: mm.display platform.linux.display
platform-provider: mm.touch platform.linux.touch
platform-provider: mm.imu platform.linux.imu
---

# Native AArch64 Linux SDK

The hosted AArch64 Linux lane. It intentionally has no runtime-prefix: the
native compiler uses the running system's libc and loader.

compiler-family: any because this SDK supplies no specs file, no linker script,
and no runtime prefix. It owns none of the link, so it constrains none of the
toolchain: a lane may select gcc or clang and the SDK is equally true of both.
A bare-metal SDK cannot say this, and the loader rejects it there.
